  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You are given a rooted tree with NNN nodes (numbered 111 through NNN); the root is node 111. For each valid iii, node iii has weight wiw_iwi​, which is either 000 or 111.\n\nWe want to traverse the tree using depth first search. The order in which the nodes are visited is not uniquely defined, since we may visit the children of each node in an arbitrary order. Formally, the pseudocode of DFS-traversal is:\n\n`function DFS(node n):\r\n\tnode n is visited\r\n\tfor each node s (s is a son of n) in some order:\r\n\t\tcall DFS(s)\r\n\treturn\r\ncall DFS(root)\n`For each possible DFS-traversal of the tree, consider the sequence of weights of nodes in the order in which they are visited; each node is visited exactly once, so this sequence has length NNN. Calculate the number of inversions for each such sequence. The minimum of these numbers is the treeversion of our tree.\n\nFind the treeversion of the given tree.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1,0001 \\le T \\le 1,0001≤T≤1,000",
      "1≤N≤1051 \\le N \\le 10^51≤N≤105",
      "0≤wi≤10 \\le w_i \\le 10≤wi​≤1 for each valid iii",
      "1≤x,y≤N1 \\le x, y \\le N1≤x,y≤N",
      "the graph on the input is a tree",
      "the sum of NNN over all test cases does not exceed 10610^6106",
      "Subtasks**Subtask #1 (50 points)**:",
      "1≤N≤1,0001 \\le N \\le 1,0001≤N≤1,000",
      "the sum of NNN over all test cases does not exceed 10,00010,00010,000"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "The first line of the input contains a single integer TTT denoting the number of test cases. The description of TTT test cases follows.\nThe first line of each test case contains a single integer NNN.\nThe second line contains NNN space-separated integers w1,w2,…,wNw_1, w_2, \\ldots, w_Nw1​,w2​,…,wN​.\nEach of the following N−1N-1N−1 lines contains two space-separated integers xxx and yyy denoting that nodes xxx and yyy are connected by an edge.",
    "outputFormat": "For each test case, print a single line containing one integer — the treeversion of the given tree.",
